00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:21.300
A covered call ETF approach lets investors sell 30 delta monthly calls on QQQ or XIU to collect 8 to 12 percent annualized deals on top of any capital appreciation

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:33.520
Implementation starts on platforms like Questrade or Interactive Brokers by selecting the broad equity ETF and selling the calls at the 30 delta strike each month

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:42.880
The premium arrives regardless of modest upside, but the main risk is opportunity cost if the underlying rally sharply above the strike

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:51.660
Size the covered calls so they represent no more than 20 to 30 percent of total equity exposure to preserve upside participation

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:59.900
This approach has historically performed best in range bound or mildly bullish markets where the underlying drift sideways

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:10.400
